  "answer_text": "You can download the latest version of Python from the **official Python website**. Here are the details:\n\n### \ud83d\udc0d Latest Version: Python 3.14.5\nThe latest version is **Python 3.14.5**, and Python source code and installers are available for download for all versions at **[python.org](https://www.python.org/downloads/)**.\n\nPython 3.14.5 was released on **May 10, 2026**.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udce5 Download Links by Platform:\n- **All platforms (main page):** https://www.python.org/downloads/\n- **Windows:** https://www.python.org/downloads/windows/\n- **macOS:** https://www.python.org/downloads/macos/\n- **Source (Linux/Unix):** https://www.python.org/downloads/source/\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\ude9f Note for Windows Users:\nThe traditional installer for Windows is being replaced by a new **Python Install Manager**, which can be installed from the Windows Store or from its download page. The install manager supports Windows 10 (or Windows Server 2022) and later, and can install versions of Python as far back as 3.5.\n\n---\n\n### \u2728 What's New in Python 3.14:\nSome major new features include free-threaded Python being officially supported (PEP 779), deferred evaluation of annotations (PEP 649), template string literals or \"t-strings\" (PEP 750), multiple interpreters in the stdlib (PEP 734), and a new `compression.zstd` module for Zstandard compression (PEP 784).\n\nAlways make sure to download Python from the **official python.org website** to ensure you're getting a safe and authentic version!",
